 "about_text": "Tokyo Gallery + BTAP is Japan's oldest contemporary art gallery, founded in Tokyo in 1950 by Yamamoto Takashi together with Shimizu Kusuo, initially as the Sukiyabashi Gallery. From the late 1950s it introduced Western abstraction, Gutai, Neo Dada and Mono-ha artists, later becoming a key champion of postwar Korean and Chinese contemporary art. In 2002 it opened BTAP in Beijing's 798 Art Zone, and in 2006 adopted its current dual name. Led today by Yamamoto Toyotsugu in Tokyo and Tabata Yukito in Beijing, the gallery continues to present postwar Japanese art alongside younger generations of artists across Japan, Korea and China, and takes part regularly in international art fairs.",
